4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T09:05:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T09:06:44Z","body":"Is there a reason not to use `Array[Projection]` instead?\nEdit: Akien sniped me :D","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3852087981/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3852141261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115858#issuecomment-3852141261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115858","id":3852141261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lmwLN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T09:13:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T09:13:49Z","body":"The only reason to add this would be for especially sensitive performance concerns, but a lot of that can be solved by just copying the data in exposed methods and using faster alternatives internally","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3852141261/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3857170284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115858#issuecomment-3857170284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115858","id":3857170284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7l579s","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-06T00:47:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T00:47:04Z","body":"I would like to recommend two approaches that can solve this issue without needing a new variant type.\r\n\r\nFirst, perhaps PackedByteArray be considered for performance reasons if arrays of projection matrices need to be exposed to GDScript compatible APIs. This would have to be an advanced API and only makes sense for large arrays, since users will have to use the PackedByteArray encode and decode functions.\r\n\r\n> This in order to pass stereo and/or multiple view projections around, including sourcing them from a GDExtension.\r\n\r\nFor such small arrays, I would suggest exposing this data as a PackedVector4Array might be simpler. Users who want to use them as projections can use the built-in `Projection(x_axis: Vector4, y_axis: Vector4, z_axis: Vector4, w_axis: Vector4)` constructor. It might take a little bit of extra conversion, but for really small arrays (for example 2 multiview projections), the performance overhead will not be significant.\r\n\r\nLong term, I think we should continue research on struct support in Godot. Then projection could be converted to a struct and packed that way perhaps.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3857170284/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910632467","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115858#issuecomment-3910632467","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115858","id":3910632467,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pF4QT","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T21:43:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T21:43:48Z","body":"> Have you considered just using `TypedArray<Projection>`?\r\n\r\nBecause I had forgotten all about that? :)\r\n\r\nI'm using that right now. Only thing I don't like about it is the overhead, but I don't think its a big deal.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910632467/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910642331","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115858#issuecomment-3910642331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115858","id":3910642331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pF6qb","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-16T21:46:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-16T21:46:46Z","body":"> I would like to recommend two approaches that can solve this issue without needing a new variant type.\r\n\r\nThe thing with those sorts of solution is that it requires a bunch of explanation that we can prevent by proper typing. We actually do something similar in the internals of XR interface, inherited from Godot 3 days where we couldn't do any of this. We just passed it as an array of floats.\r\n\r\nWhile what I'm doing right now is only indirectly related, I do hope to clean up that part of the API one day. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910642331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4195945291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115858#issuecomme